    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0296" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/5–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Churchill</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Truman </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-05-05">May 5, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. I am very much obliged to you for number 25.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d209-f1"/>
                    I am also most concerned about the fate of the 15 Polish representatives in view
                    of statement made by Mr. Molotov to Stettinius at San Francisco that they had
                    been arrested by the Red Army, and I think that you and I should consult
                    together very carefully upon this matter. If these Poles were enticed into
                    Russian [hands] and are now no longer alive, one cannot quite tell how far such
                    a crime would influence the future. I am in entire agreement with Mr. Eden’s
                    views and actions. I hope he will soon pass through Washington on his homeward
                    journey and that you will talk it all over with him.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d209-f1" n="22" xml:id="d209-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed: it quoted for Churchill’s information the text of Truman’s message
                    of May 4 to Stalin, <ref target="#pg280">p. 280</ref>.</p>
            </note>
